// Producer/consumer boundary contracts.
//
// Authority: CSP (Hoare 1978), Design by Contract (Meyer 1992)
//
// A Node field that crosses a pipeline stage boundary has a production
// status: the producer may have fully resolved it, errored, left it as
// a variable, or not set it at all. The consumer's contract determines
// which statuses are acceptable.
//
// Three consumer contracts:
//   Strict    — producer guarantees resolved; non-resolved is invariant violation
//   Tolerant  — consumer handles all variants explicitly
//   Guarded   — consumer falls back with visible marker (bootstrap bridge)
//
// This vocabulary applies to all Node cross-talk fields:
//   inferred, name, children, params, return_cardinality, properties, body, match_pattern
//
// Currently only `inferred` has the full producer (InferredNode) / consumer
// (NodeType) / accessor (rt_node) triad. The others will follow as they
// are dissolved.

module std.boundary

type BoundaryContract
  = Strict
  | Tolerant
  | Guarded
